# macOS
.DS_Store

# Claude Code — machine-local settings (keep shared skills tracked)
.claude/settings.local.json

# Source screenshots for Glimmers entries — deliberately NOT tracked.
#
# Netlify serves this repo root as-is and robots.txt is Allow: /, so a tracked
# PNG is live and crawlable at a bare URL. The committed JPEGs are downscaled and
# sit inside an essay that states their provenance; the full-resolution originals
# at context-free URLs would be closer to hosting somebody's footage than to
# illustrating an argument — and SpaceX's licence for webcast frames is precisely
# the thing FACTCHECK.md records that we could NOT establish.
#
# The PNG is also not the original. It is a screenshot, itself a derivative. The
# archive is the broadcast at a timestamp, and FACTCHECK.md records those to the
# second; going back to the video beats anything recoverable from a saved frame.
#
# Keep the originals outside the repo. If a page ever needs one, commit a
# downscaled JPEG that a page actually references, as the four current ones are.
nancy-grace-roman-space-telescope-launch*.png
